export anchor TwoSidebarsStyle:
    number: 177
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Two sidebars
    idea: A three-column workspace with labelled navigation on the left, a centre feed of project cards with progress rings, and a pale green context panel on the right holding the week chart and an activity timeline, cool white with one green.
    base: light
    palette:
        page: #f6f8fa, the cool white page behind the feed
        paper: #ffffff, the left sidebar, project cards, top bars, chips and the chart well
        context: #eef4f1, the right context panel
        ink: #18232b, text
        muted: #55636e, meta, labels, section captions and day letters
        line: #dfe5ea, card borders and dividers
        green: #146c43, the primary button, links, the current nav item, rings, this week bars, timeline nodes, On track and focus
        greenSoft: #e3f2ea, the current nav item fill
        ringTrack: #dfe8e3, the empty part of progress rings
        lastWeek: #7f9a8b, outlines of last week bars
        risk: #8b5000, At risk text and triangle
        bad: #b02a1e, Behind and overdue text, crossed square, clock and the overdue chip
    type:
        One stack, Segoe UI, system-ui, Roboto, Helvetica Neue, Arial. Base
        14px at 1.5. The greeting is 24px bold, project names 15px at 650,
        the feed heading 16px bold, panel captions and nav groups 11 to 13px
        bold caps tracked 0.08em, chip figures 16px bold, week totals 22px
        bold, meta 13px and ring figures 11px bold.
    layout:
        Three full-height columns of 232px, the flexible centre and 344px.
        The white left sidebar holds a green rounded square mark and the
        wordmark, a Workspace caption over six icon and label nav items with
        Home filled pale green and a count of 6 beside Projects, and a Needs
        attention group linking Billing migration and Mobile app 2.0 with
        their status. The centre has a white top bar with a wide search
        field and a green New project button, then the greeting, date and
        red overdue line, then the four figures as rounded pill chips in one
        row, overdue in pale red with a clock. Under a Projects heading the
        feed is six separate white cards, each with a 44px green progress
        ring holding the percent, name over category and task count, due
        date over days left, and the status at the right end. The pale green
        right panel starts with a bell and Mara Okafor, then a Tasks
        completed caption, two small white tiles with last week 59 and this
        week 73 up 14, the fourteen-day bar chart in a white well with
        outlined last week bars and green this week bars, and an Activity
        timeline down a vertical line with hollow green nodes. Below 1200px
        the right panel drops under the feed as two columns. Below 760px the
        nav becomes a three by two grid, the bell and user sit top right,
        and everything stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 32px centre gutters, 20px panel padding, 8px between feed cards, 12 to 16px card padding.
    density: Medium. Three columns of context at once, roomy cards in the centre.
    corners: Rounded. 8px cards, buttons, fields and tiles, 12px on the style sheet, pill chips, round rings and nodes.
    borders: 1px cool grey borders on cards, chips and sidebars. The right panel uses pale green edged tiles.
    shadows: None. Columns separate by tone, white left, cool white centre, pale green right.
    icons:
        Line icons at 1.8px stroke, 18px, muted in the nav and green when
        current. Status uses a check circle for On track, a triangle for At
        risk, a crossed square for Behind and a clock for overdue, always
        with the word.
    focus: A 2px green outline offset 2px on every control.
    tone: Friendly and plain, with lowercase chip labels such as tasks due this week and short captions such as Needs attention.
